## Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: Is this about making Chrome compliant?**

No. This workshop demonstrates systemic governance failure requiring regulatory capacity innovation, not vendor-specific fixes.

**Q: Who developed TPI-R methodology?**

TPI-R methodology derives from Kantara ANCR WG and Kantara MVCR (Consent Receipt Specification), adopted as ISO/IEC 27560 consent record information structure and specified in accordance with Convention 108+ transparency conduct requirements for cross-border data transfers.

**Q: What happens after the workshop?**

Q2 2026 CoE consultation and Q3 2026 UN/CEFACT liaison will advance international coordination. GitHub repository provides technical implementation resources.

**Q: What is Multi-Lateral Governance?**

Distributed enforcement capacity across jurisdictions with decentralized transparency infrastructure. Enables coordinated regulatory action without centralized control.

**Q: How does this relate to GDPR/PIPEDA/other regulations?**

Standards-based transparency infrastructure is compatible with all major privacy frameworks. Convention 108+ integration ensures broad jurisdictional coverage.

